		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"690A67A6D21199B1"
				"3AC9A7994C4F9DC0"
			]
			description: [
				"Fluids sit on the same heat scale as fires: water is &3Cold&r, lava &6Hot&r, molten metal as hot as it melts. Every pipe, pump and tank has a ceiling: brass, glass, copper and iron take up to &6Hot&r, steel &cSearing&r, aluminium only &eWarm&r and PVC only &3Cold&r. Past it, a part glows, then bursts or melts and spills."
				""
				"Plain pipes only join pipes of their own metal. Pumps, valves and smart pipes join anything, so use one as the adapter. Tanks of different metals never join."
				""
				"Tooltips say how hot a fluid each part takes."
			]
			id: "361F092D54BF5055"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Fluids are hot or cold too"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7430378DE8182367"
